  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Security fix: sensitive HTTP headers are now redacted in diagnostic output.\n\n\t\t\tPreviously AuthenticatedHttpClientHandler joined every request and response header, key and\n\t\t\tvalue, into its Debug level log message. The handler sets an Authorization header carrying the\n\t\t\tAPI token, base64 encoded, on every request, so a usable credential was written verbatim and was\n\t\t\ttrivially recoverable by decoding it. Any consumer running at Debug retained usable credentials\n\t\t\tfor the life of its log store, and a Toggl API token does not expire.\n\n\t\t\tAuthorization, Proxy-Authorization, Cookie, Set-Cookie and common API key headers are now\n\t\t\tredacted, case-insensitively, on request and response, along with any vendor-prefixed variant\n\t\t\twhose name ends in \"Authorization\". The scheme and credential length are retained, so requests\n\t\t\tremain diagnosable. The log line format is otherwise unchanged.\n\n\t\t\tConsumers should upgrade, review existing Debug logs for previously captured tokens, and\n\t\t\tregenerate any token that appears in them.\n\n\t\t\tBreaking Change: Renamed all \"Me\" references to \"CurrentUser\".\n\t\t\tNote: Toggl have crippled their API, limiting even Premium users to 600 API calls per hour.\n\t\t\tBeyond that, you will receive HTTP 402 \"Payment Required\" response - this is an incorrect HTTP Status - it should be 429 \"Too Many Requests\".\n\t\t\tYou can provide your feedback to Toggl here: https://community.toggl.com/",
